# Prisma
# NOTE: migration SQL is intentionally NOT ignored.
# This used to read `packages/api/prisma/migrations/*/migration.sql`, which
# silently dropped every new migration from every commit — `git add` said
# nothing and the file simply never landed. The one migration in the repo
# predates that rule, so it survived and the breakage stayed invisible: the
# schema kept evolving in schema.prisma while the migration history could not,
# which is how ~115 columns and a whole table ended up existing only in the
# datamodel. Migration SQL is source of truth for the database and must be
# committed.

